@startuml
title Transfer restriction - core mint / burn
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false

start
:mint(account, value) / batchMint(accounts, values)\nburn(account, value) / batchBurn(accounts, values);
if (contract deactivated?) then (yes)
  :revert EnforcedDeactivation;
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (account frozen?) then (yes)
  :revert ERC7943CannotReceive(to)   [mint]\nor ERC7943CannotSend(from)   [burn];
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (RuleEngine set?) then (yes)
  :RuleEngine.transferred(...)\n(reverts if not compliant);
else (no)
endif
:mint / burn valid -> rest of the ERC-20 flow;
stop

note right
  Mint and burn are NOT blocked by pause - only by deactivation.
  To burn from a frozen address, the issuer must use
  forcedBurn / forcedTransfer (ERC20Enforcement).
end note
@enduml
